  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-b48de8f4-7fff-c76b-4fef-45002f00d974&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:12pt;margin-bottom:12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;The proposed advertisement, by reason of its inappropriate scale and location on this narrowed section of public highway, would give rise to adverse obstruction of pedestrian and user movement, including for people with mobility impairments, thereby harming accessibility and public safety. The development is therefore contrary to Policies PP1 (Public Realm), LP2 (Development and Amenity), LP7 (Advertisements), LP41 Liveable Neighbourhoods), LP42 (Walking and Cycling) and LP43 (Transport and Development) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033, Policies D8 (Public Realm), T1 (Strategic Approach to Transport), T2 (Healthy Streets) of the London Plan (2021), Hackney Shopfront Design Guide and Hackneys Transport Strategy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
